+# Five-point spline road blocks — 2026-10-06
+
+Owner request: add a road block fitted through exactly five points, with a configurable road width at every point and interpolation between points. Requirement IDs: R01, T01–T04, V03–V05, Q01; local acceptance items SP01 (five-point fitting), SP02 (point widths), SP03 (editor/persistence/compilation).
+
+Track → Spline creates one ordinary road block. Drag any of its five numbered dots to reshape it; the fitted road passes through all five points. Tap a numbered dot, or cycle **Point n/5**, to select its width. Drag the cyan width handle or use **Width − / Width +** (0.5 m increments). Width values retain the existing 6–20 m road limits. Drag inside to move the whole block; Flip mirrors it; Confirm, Snap, Connect, Delete, undo/redo and atomic draft/original saves use the existing editor flow. When editing a selected spline, start-line overlay controls yield to the point handles; the actual start-line road paint and its Track tool remain available.
+
+## Geometry and contract
+
+`SplineRoad` uses deterministic centripetal Catmull–Rom tangents and cubic Hermite evaluation across four spans. Endpoints use one-sided tangents. Every span includes its exact authored endpoint, so all five interpolation points remain represented in the sampled geometry. Width interpolates linearly by distance along each sampled span, without width overshoot. Adjacent control points must be at least 2 m apart; finite world samples must remain inside the existing ±120 m map bounds. Existing piece/road-length budgets remain active.
+
+The additive `creator-track-v5` spline variant stores `spline_points` (five local coordinate pairs) and `point_widths` (five widths). The first local point is `[0,0]`; moving it rebases the local frame and keeps the other four world points fixed. The existing position/heading/flip fields control the whole block. `width` is the maximum point width for conservative bounds. Endpoint poses use the actual fitted tangent, and connected mouth matching uses actual endpoint widths rather than that maximum. Join width blending ends before the next internal interpolation point, preserving all three internal widths. Other block geometry retains its existing behavior.
+
+`RoadPieces.section_geometry` supplies the same spline/width samples to rendering, outlines/kerbs, rasterized drivable surfaces, roadside runs and automatic routing. Start-line placement uses the local interpolated width. No manual waypoints are added. Tight user-shaped roads can still produce folded offset edges, as with existing sharp curves; this block does not introduce a road clearance or minimum bend-radius rule.
+
+Compiler version advances from **creator-compiler-20 to creator-compiler-21**, and both game and canonical verifier use the new helper. The standalone verifier staging allowlist includes it. The authoring schema JSON adds bounded spline fields and variant conditions; existing v5 documents still load without migration or deletion. Compiler/hash golden identities change; original geometry, recorded input frames, physics/rules versions, times and lap assertions remain intact. In particular the existing verified oval fixture changes only `expected_manifest.compiler_version` and `expected_manifest.track_content_hash`; its stored recording and 12,757-tick race remain unchanged.
+
+## Actual checks and evidence
+
+Pinned engine: `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf`, through `scripts/dev.ps1`. Desktop graphical runs use Compatibility/OpenGL on RTX 3090.
+
+- `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 Import`: initial sandbox run failed on certificate-store access; approved rerun exited 0. Engine/profile warnings were retained. New helper/test UIDs were generated.
+- `... TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_spline_road.gd -Graphical`: final **479 checks, zero failures**. Includes exact five-point fitting, distance-based widths, smooth internal tangents, malformed/nonfinite/count/range rejection, mirror/rotation/independent dragging, forward/reversed mouth widths, bounded blending, drivable cross-sections, exact JSON compilation, complete five-lap driving and replay, real touch/toolbar width controls, one-operation undo/redo, save/load, pinch rollback, first-point/start-line hit testing, ghost confirmation and inspected 1280×720/960×540 captures. Spline race: **five laps, 13,517 ticks, zero contacts**.
+- `... TestWorkflow`: **252 checks, zero failures**, including the new ghost point and committed width-handle checks. Existing generic tests assumed every block had a radius and single width handle; spline cases now exercise their own actual controls while retaining the existing position/tangent/undo assertions.
+- `... Validate -CommandTimeoutSeconds 600`: final run (`Validate-31324`) parses **309 scripts / zero failures**; spline **476 headless**, workflow **252**, road **377**, creator **113**, performance/equivalence **1215**, editor review **51**, construction **112**, App **99**, and the intervening driving/surface/record/ghost/camera/catalog suites pass. It then stops at the separate menu-loading test: `TrackBrowser._show_detail` calls nonexistent `test_drivers_available` on its `DelayedBoard` fixture. **Full Validate is not reported as green**, and later components were not run. No menu-loading/rail implementation was changed by this task. The final focused graphical spline run after the start-line-overlay correction passes **479 checks**. The earlier broad attempt (`Validate-27056`) stopped on the generic workflow's nonexistent single spline width handle; corrected without removing its substantive assertion.
+- `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest backend/tests/test_verifier.py -q -x`: **42 passed / one failed**, stopped at the separate existing HTTP-refresh peer test (`401 refresh then retry succeeds` / `retry keeps mutation key`). Spline validation/malformed-data cases and updated compiler/hash identities passed. No HTTP client implementation was changed by this task.
+- Same backend suite with `-k 'not godot_http_adapter_refreshes_without_losing_idempotency'`: **61 passed / one failed / one deselected**. This exposed the missing new helper in the standalone packaging allowlist (90 s verification timeout); fixed by including `spline_road`.
+- Final backend `-k 'standalone_verifier or spline'`: **7 passed / 56 deselected**, including real packaged-project validation for both the existing oval and new spline, real five-lap oval replay, and malformed-spline rejection. Batch counts overlap. Existing Starlette deprecation warning retained. The unrelated HTTP-refresh failure is not reported as green.
+- JSON schema formal-validator attempt was unavailable: neither local Python environment has `jsonschema`; no dependency was installed. A Python JSON/declaration audit passes for the spline enum, exact five-point/five-width counts, `[0,0]` origin and 6–20 m width bounds. Real native/backend domain validation is tested above.
+
+Initial new-test errors were corrected: a nonexistent diagnostic `surface_at` call became the actual `cell_at` boundary; saved-coordinate comparison uses saved JSON precision; a start-line fixture created a non-String key through dot assignment and now uses the contract's String key. The backend publication fixture originally lacked a placed start line; the final fixture includes it. No invariant was weakened to obtain a passing result.
+
+Evidence: [desktop spline](evidence/spline-road-2026-10-06/spline-1280x720.png), [compact spline](evidence/spline-road-2026-10-06/spline-960x540.png), [palette](evidence/spline-road-2026-10-06/palette.png), generated authoring document, copied command logs and scoped source checkpoint under `docs/evidence/spline-road-2026-10-06/`. The test stores only isolated synthetic drafts and cleans its own temporary directory; player files are preserved.
+
+Checkpoint command: `python docs/evidence/spline-road-2026-10-06/create_checkpoint.py`, followed by `git apply --reverse --check docs/evidence/spline-road-2026-10-06/scoped-change.patch` and scoped `git diff --check`: final exit 0 for each. Initial patch validation failed because Windows text output converted patch lines to CRLF; the saved patch now explicitly uses LF. The patch reconstructs only this task's edits in memory and preserves pre-existing topology preparation in its mixed helper hunk; it does not stage or commit unrelated shared-workspace changes.
+
+## Changed files and remaining acceptance
+
+Runtime: new `game/editor/spline_road.gd` and UID; `road_pieces.gd`, `editor_canvas.gd`, `editor_button.gd`, `start_line.gd`, `track_compiler.gd`; `game/core/app.gd`; `backend/deploy/stage_verifier.py`.
+
+Contracts/tests: `docs/schemas/creator-track-v5.schema.json`; new `game/tests/test_spline_road.gd` and UID / `tests/fixtures/spline_circuit.json`; `test_road_pieces.gd`, `test_creator.gd`, `test_editor_workflow.gd`; `backend/tests/test_verifier.py` / `fixtures/verified_oval.json`; `scripts/dev.ps1` (adds spline tests to Validate). Documentation: this file, `DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md` and `docs/PHASE_0_PLAN.md`.
+
+No phone attachment check, Android export/install or physical-device test was performed. Owner visual/usability acceptance and mobile performance with many spline blocks remain outstanding. No cloud/NAS/backend service deployment was performed. This build requires a separately authorized matching backend compiler rollout for online use: the client rejects cloud revisions pinned to compiler20, so existing cloud tracks also need current immutable compiler revisions before racing in this build. The compiler version deliberately changes content identities; no live published documents or records were rewritten. Unrelated concurrent backend, privacy, rivalry, race-flow, editor-performance and desert work is preserved in the shared working tree and excluded from the scoped patch.
